        "problem": "Police arrest a suspect, secure a cellphone, then open its stored messages without a warrant solely because the phone was on the suspect. Analyze whether the asserted search-incident-to-arrest basis suffices and what other facts could change the result.\n\nWRITTEN WORK: Submit a 400-word balanced IRAC analysis and a short counterargument. Name the primary statute or judicial authority that requires verification.\n\nWRITTEN EVALUATION: Produce a 700–900 word IRAC/CREAC discussion with primary-authority checks, the best contrary argument and an alternative conclusion under changed facts. Self-check responses do not grade substantive writing.",
